# An allowlist: deny everything, then admit only what the six service binaries
# import, which `go list -deps` over ./cmd/taskforge-{api,outbox,scheduler,
# reconciler,worker,migrate} shows is go.mod, go.sum, cmd/, internal/ and
# migrations/. Nothing else enters the build context: not .git, not .env, not the
# SDK, the dashboard source, the docs or node_modules.
#
# internal/ includes internal/dashboard/dist, which the api embeds. It is
# gitignored apart from .gitkeep, and Docker's ignore file does not read
# .gitignore, so this allowlist is what lets the built dashboard in. `make images`
# runs `make dash-build` first so that there is one to admit.
#
# dashboard/Dockerfile has its own allowlist beside it (Dockerfile.dockerignore),
# which BuildKit prefers for that file, so the two do not interact.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!internal
!migrations
# Tests are not part of an image's build.
**/*_test.go
